The fastcgi transport now wraps a failed dial as a `reverseproxy.DialError`, so `lb_try_duration` retries it for every method, as the HTTP transport already does. I haven't compiled this or run any tests, including the repro from the issue.

`DialError` embeds the unexported `error` field, so code outside `reverseproxy` can't build one with `DialError{err}`, and the suggestion in the issue wouldn't compile. I added an exported `NewDialError` constructor in `reverseproxy.go` and call it from `fastcgi.go`. The error message changes only slightly: it still reads `dialing backend: ...`, but now wraps the cause with `%w` instead of `%v`.

